# 1️⃣ Stack using Array

## 📖 Idea

Store stack elements in an array and maintain a **Top** index.

---

### Visualization

```
        TOP
         ↓
    +-------+
    |   40  |
    +-------+
    |   30  |
    +-------+
    |   20  |
    +-------+
    |   10  |
    +-------+
```

---

### C++ Implementation

```cpp
class Stack
{
    int arr[100];
    int top;

public:

    Stack()
    {
        top = -1;
    }

    void push(int x)
    {
        arr[++top] = x;
    }

    void pop()
    {
        if(top != -1)
            top--;
    }

    int peek()
    {
        return arr[top];
    }

    bool empty()
    {
        return top == -1;
    }
};
```

---

### Complexity

| Operation | Time |
|-----------|------|
| Push | O(1) |
| Pop | O(1) |
| Peek | O(1) |

